  "limitations": [
    "Development diagnostic on the executed fixed-gamma-7 trajectory, not independent held-out policy evaluation.",
    "The perfect-prefix reference uses future accepted prefixes from this same step. It is not implementable online.",
    "Cap changes can change subsequent tokens, proposals, KV state, batching and execution costs. Those changed trajectories are not simulated or verified.",
    "Cost comes from separate budget-7 complete synchronous host-step calibration cells or the existing within-range batch interpolation; it is not this counterfactual step's measured cost.",
    "A score is calibrated step cost divided by mean per-request progress, not measured effective TPOT, end-to-end policy performance or a theoretical bound.",
    "Do not convert mean scores or their gaps into an end-to-end speedup; never plot these as measured policy curves in F3.",
    "No extra draft is invented beyond the observed full offer. Accepted-prefix truncation is used only on identifiable, nonterminal request outputs.",
    "Replayed pre-step choices use the existing estimator and cost policy with a cold prior once per run; they are not actually executed adaptive choices. Unlogged warmup state is not reconstructed.",
    "Steps, requests and ranks share an execution trajectory and are not independent system repetitions. Raw run-level summaries are retained.",
    "The single-run calibrated cap-cost differences are nonmonotone; small action-ranking gaps include unresolved calibration variation.",
    "Per-run replay score summaries coincide across the two measured trajectory repeats. This is not evidence of independent uncertainty vanishing.",
    "Small score gaps do not establish that online information has no value or that complete-policy improvement has no remaining opportunity.",
    "Complete synchronous host step includes current verification, next draft generation and host/controller work. No async component arithmetic, HBM inference or causal budget-tax estimate.",
    "All comparisons use compiled data; no eager trajectory or cost enters the analysis.",
    "Both campaigns have matching runner/plugin/cost-model source hashes. Fixed-G7 calibration has64 output tokens/request and one run/cell; native G=gamma has128 tokens and two runs. General warmup offsets are0 versus80, with shape warmup0 in both; time windows differ.",
    "Pure-cost ranks ignore accepted progress and are not claims of optimal actions or measured policy performance. Small nonmonotone single-run differences have no established statistical ordering.",
    "B1 replay and perfect-prefix gaps are zero because this table's cap7 is both the lowest-cost cap and has weakly maximal identified progress on this fixed trace. This is conditional on the single-run table, not evidence of globally optimal online control."
